Today is Saturday evening.
I am going to Priya's house for dinner.
I think that I will buy some sweets for her.
I stop at a bright mithai shop near the station.
There are many fresh sweets here.
I see Kaju Katli behind the glass.
I go near the counter.
"Bhaiya, how much is the Kaju Katli?" I ask the shopkeeper.
"Madam, it is one thousand rupees a kilo," he tells me.
"Please pack half a kilo of Kaju Katli," I say.
"Will you pack it in a nice box?" I ask.
"Yes madam, I will pack it right now," he replies.
He puts the sweet in a beautiful red box.
He gives the box to me.
I give him five hundred rupees.
"Thank you, bhaiya," I say smiling.
Now let's go to the metro station.
I know that Priya will be very happy.
